Yeah. The shared zeitgeist is the part of your private memory a stranger can recognize.

Think about the sound of a dial-up modem. Somebody remembers waiting to talk to their crush on AIM. Somebody else remembers their mom yelling to get off the internet because she needed the phone. They can both hear that sound today and go, Oh, I know exactly where I am.

And there were smaller zeitgeists inside that one. Your house had its own rules. Your friend group had its own jokes. You and Tyler could hear the same sound, remember the same room, and each bring up a detail the other had completely forgotten. That’s what I like about the communal part. Sometimes another person can give you back a piece of your own past.